From e33a87d7e74d46cd0b4ccca4554cf485b60bd2e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 02:37:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris, venus: fixes for hardware video encode on QCS6490 / Radxa Dragon Q6A
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Series for Radxa linux-7.0.11 (base a50eb5b71). Details, root causes,
evidence and the test plan: docs/q6a-video/FIXES.md in the linux-qcom repo.

 1-4   Iris: upstream fixes missing from 7.0.11 (cherry-picked, authorship kept)
 5-8   Venus: upstream parser and encoder-step fixes (cherry-picked)
 9-12  Iris: runtime-PM / clock-unwind / command-queue bugs
 13    Iris: keep the IRQ thread off the registers after power-off
       (replaces upstream b9c2215bdedc, which can deadlock on this tree)
 14-17 Iris: teardown / open() error handling
 18-21 Iris encoder: frame size, crop/selection, frame rate
 22-25 Iris: firmware detection, diagnostics, probe order, DMA warning

Status: every commit builds with clang 18 (LLVM=1, arm64, W=1, no warnings) with
Iris built as a module, and the Venus patches also with CONFIG_VIDEO_QCOM_IRIS=n;
checkpatch is clean apart from the trailers; the clang static analyzer reports
nothing on the touched files; three of the bugs are reproduced and shown fixed
with user-space replays (docs/q6a-video/tests). NOTHING HAS BEEN RUN ON
HARDWARE. The submitter needs to add Signed-off-by before sending upstream.

Bryan O'Donoghue (1):
  media: iris: Enumerate cap->bus_info to differentiate between encoder
    and decoder

Claude (17):
  media: qcom: iris: fix runtime PM reference leaks in power domain
    helpers
  media: qcom: iris: fix clock unwind in iris_vpu_power_on_hw()
  media: qcom: iris: don't drop a runtime PM reference that was never
    taken
  media: qcom: iris: treat a completely full HFI command queue as full
  media: qcom: iris: keep the IRQ thread off the registers once power is
    off
  media: qcom: iris: handle runtime PM resume failure in core deinit
  media: qcom: iris: bound the wait for system error recovery
  media: qcom: iris: return queued capture buffers on an early
    stop_streaming
  media: qcom: iris: fix error handling when opening a video node
  media: qcom: iris: validate the encoder frame size in try_fmt
  media: qcom: iris: make encoder crop selection consistent
  media: qcom: iris: round the encoder frame rate to the nearest integer
  media: qcom: iris: don't memcpy a format onto itself in the encoder
  media: qcom: iris: don't read past the end of the firmware when
    detecting Gen2
  media: qcom: iris: say why the firmware could not be loaded
  media: qcom: iris: publish the video nodes only once the device is
    usable
  media: qcom: iris: warn when the SC7280 DT node lacks dma-coherent

Dikshita Agarwal (2):
  media: qcom: iris: Fix bitmask test in iris_allow_cmd()
  media: qcom: iris: fix state-change debug log printing stale value

Mohammed EL Kadiri (2):
  media: venus: fix payload size calculation in parse_raw_formats()
  media: venus: fix payload size returned by parse_caps() and
    parse_alloc_mode()

Renjiang Han (2):
  media: qcom: venus: relax encoder frame/blur step size on v6
  media: qcom: venus: relax encoder frame/blur dimension steps on v4

Wangao Wang (1):
  media: qcom: iris: fix missing hfi_id in gen1 GOP_SIZE cap

